Tag names follow the language, and 36 more strings become translatable

Reported as: tag names do not change with the language.

Tags were translated everywhere except the settings table, which showed
the raw base name. That was deliberate — it is the field you edit — but
when it is the one place still in Persian it reads as the translation
being broken. The table shows the name in the current language now, with
the base name beneath it when they differ.

Chasing that turned up a third blind spot in the key extractor: Persian
literals returned straight from a function, like the per-type field
labels in domain/tags/groups.ts. It saw neither those nor, therefore, the
36 error messages written the same way — "the amount is not valid", "a
timer is already running", "you do not have access for this" — all of
which stayed Persian in every language while the checker reported zero
missing.

Also: the access column and the kanban/pipeline labels went out
untranslated for the same reason as `header` earlier — a hardcoded
Persian label passed as data, never through t(). And the group column is
dropped for tag types that have no groups instead of showing a column of
dashes.

